WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.484
Hiring an outside engineer is scary for one reason: you don't know what happens after you sign. So here's exactly how I work — no mystery.

00:08.484 --> 00:17.529
Four stages. We start with a one-week audit — you get a plan either way. Then a scoped sprint. Then the build, in the open. Then I operate it, so it keeps working.

00:17.529 --> 00:28.942
What makes it safe: fixed scope, so no surprise invoices. A working demo every week, so you're never in the dark. And you own everything — code, tests, and docs — from day one.

00:28.942 --> 00:35.712
The result is predictable, visible, and yours: shipped on time, proven before it ships, with no lock-in.

00:35.712 --> 00:40.291
Know exactly what you're getting — before you commit. Start with the audit.

